for a single to be led to use my 2. If they play other combinations (straights, triples), I may never get to play.\n2. **Play Single 2**: This leaves me with a pair of 9s. Since the 2 is the highest single, it can only be beaten by a Bomb. Reviewing the unknown cards, only the rank of 4 has four cards remaining (count: 4). Thus, the only hand that can stop me is a Bomb of 4s. If the opponents do not have 4444, the 2 will win the trick, and I can then play the pair of 9s to win the game immediately.\n\nReason: Playing the 2 first sets up a forced win sequence unless an opponent holds the specific Bomb of 4s. Playing the 9s first surrenders control almost guaranteed, significantly lowering the win rate.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦2"]}'}
